# `todo/t1077` NO-OP CELL — a BARE `Box[Box[T]]` PARAMETER. This one is GREEN
# BEFORE THE FIX AND GREEN AFTER, and it is here to STAY green.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT RED-VERIFY THIS FIXTURE, AND DO NOT "FIX" IT. It is the one cell in
# the class that the pre-fix compiler got RIGHT, and it got it right BY
# ACCIDENT (six-questions #6): a `Box[T]` parameter is represented internally
# as `*Box__T`, so the pre-fix gate `is_box(deref_type)` — which tests the
# RESULT of the first peel — happened to agree with the correct gate
# `ptr_to_box` — which tests the SOURCE — for exactly this shape. Two peels are
# genuinely needed here, and two peels are what both gates ask for.
#
#   PRE-fix,  C and LLVM: build rc 0, run rc 0, prints `42` / `hi!`
#   POST-fix, C and LLVM: build rc 0, run rc 0, prints `42` / `hi!`
#
# ⚠ IT IS ALSO A TRAP FOR THE NEXT PERSON WHO REVERTS THE FIX TO RE-MEASURE.
# Revert the gate, run THIS fixture, see green, and you will conclude the
# revert did not take. It did — you picked the one cell that cannot show it.
# The cells that CAN are every other `box_nested_deref_*.gg` in this directory.
#
# ⭐ Its real job: the fix narrows the second peel from `is_box(deref_type)` to
# `ptr_to_box`, and the two conditions differ in EXACTLY ONE cell (`Box__T`
# where T is itself a box). This fixture pins the OTHER side of that boundary —
# the cell where the second peel must still happen. Without it, "narrow the
# gate" and "delete the gate" look the same to the test suite.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: 42 then hi!
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.
#
# ⛔ `known_gaps/` with a LIVE test: the self-host cannot compile nested `Box`
# at all (`todo/t1311`), and top level is auto-scanned into
# `runtime_parity_corpus`. Unlike its siblings this cell is a no-op rather than
# a fix, but it shares their placement for the same self-host reason.

void show_int(Box[Box[int]] w):
    print((*(*w)))

void show_str(Box[Box[String]] w):
    print((*(*w)))

void main():
    Box[Box[int]] a = Box[Box[int]](Box[int](42))
    show_int(a)
    Box[Box[String]] b = Box[Box[String]](Box[String]("hi" + "!"))
    show_str(b)
